# UxPlay defaults — Silver Goggles (KDE Wayland / Dell G15 5520, RTX 3060)
#
# Format: one option per line, WITHOUT the leading "-" of the command-line flag.
# Installed to ~/.config/uxplayrc by `ujust airplay-setup` (never overwritten).
# Full reference: `man uxplay` or `uxplay -h`.

n Silver Goggles

# Fixed "legacy" ports (TCP 7100,7000,7001 / UDP 6000,6001,7011). Without this,
# UxPlay picks ports at random, which no firewall rule can anticipate.
p

# Client authentication. `pin` shows a 4-digit code on the terminal for every new
# client; `reg` persists authenticated clients to ~/.uxplay.register so trusted
# devices are not re-prompted. Dropping both makes any host on the LAN able to
# mirror onto this screen unprompted.
pin
reg

# Wayland compositor + PipeWire audio (both confirmed present in the base image).
vs waylandsink
as pipewiresink

# NVDEC h264 decoding on the RTX 3060, via the GStreamer `nvcodec` plugin
# (gstreamer1-plugins-bad-free + libcuda). Comment out to fall back to decodebin's
# own choice, or use `vd avdec_h264` to force software decoding.
vd nvh264dec

# Inhibit the screensaver while UxPlay runs, over the org.freedesktop.ScreenSaver
# D-Bus service. Upstream notes this may not take effect on Wayland.
scrsv 2

# Uncomment for pure screen mirroring (second-monitor / webcam use): drops
# timestamp-based A/V sync for lower latency. Leave commented when mirroring
# video that needs audio kept in sync.
# vsync no
